---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<section class="mb-5">
		<h1>Opus Consultation</h1>
	</section>
	<section>
		<div class="separation">
			<p>Thank you for your visit, it was a pleasure meeting you. Today we discussed your Opus treatment.</p>
			<p>Below are a few pre-treatment considerations; if applicable.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>What is Opus</h2>
			<p>OPUS is a non-invasive radiofrequency (RF) treatment designed to improve skin texture and enhance facial tightening. Utilizing fractional RF technology together with Opus Plasma applicator, it addresses a wide range of skin concerns, from mild to more complex issues. It can help with skin resurfacing, skin rejuvenation, scar revision, wrinkle reduction and helps with skin laxity.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Hyperpigmentation Prevention</h2>
			<p>Patients with darker skin tones (especially Fitzpatrick skin types IV–V), If recommended by your provider, hydroquinone 4% may be used twice daily for 4–6 weeks before treatment to reduce the risk of post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation. Then Stop HQ 1 week prior to treatment.</p>
			<p>Topical retinoids (such as tretinoin) and actives (such as glycolic acid) products may improve treatment preparation; however, these products are typically discontinued 5–7 days before treatment unless otherwise directed.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Precautions</h2>
			<p>Do not use this technology over Neurotoxin or Restylane for two weeks post injection.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Cold Sore Prevention</h2>
			<p>Patients with a history of cold sores (HSV-1) may be prescribed antiviral medication (such as valacyclovir) beginning 24 hours before treatment and continuing for the duration recommended by your provider.</p>
			<p>Avoid tanning and excessive sun exposure for at least 2–4 weeks before treatment. Daily use of a Mineral SPF 50 sunscreen is strongly recommended.</p>
		</div>

		<div class="separation">
			<h2>Contraindications for Treatment</h2>
			<p>	• Burns <br>
				• Have a history of poor wound healing. <br>
				• Antibiotic or Steroid in the past 2 weeks <br>
				• Active bacterial or viral infections <br>
				• Metal implants <br>
				• Aneurysm clips <br>
				• Ablative/non-ablative cosmetic intervention in the past 3 months <br>
				• Implanted pacemaker or defibrillator <br>
				• Pregnancy or IVF procedure <br>
				• Radiation therapy <br>
				• Scleroderma <br>
				• Cancer in the past 6 months, Chemo/radiation in the past 6 months <br>
				• Active collagen or vascular disease <br>
				• Poor healing <br>
				• Impaired immune system <br>
				• Bacterial or viral infection <br>
				• Isotretinoin in the past 12 months <br>
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>
